{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":913,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Prov.26","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Proverbs","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Proverbs 26","reference":"Proverbs 26","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":2,"text":"By flying - Secures itself from the fowler.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":3,"text":"Not come - Upon the innocent person, but he shall escape from it like a bird.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":4,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":5,"text":"According - So as to imitate his folly, by passionate or reproachful speeches.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":6,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":7,"text":"According - So as his folly needs and requires, convincing him strongly, reproving him sharply, and exposing him to just shame.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":8,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":9,"text":"Cutteth off the feet - Of his messenger; bids one go that wants legs.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":10,"text":"Drinketh - Drinking, in scripture, frequently denotes the plentiful doing or receiving of any thing.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":11,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":12,"text":"The legs - Hebrew. the legs of the lame are lifted up, in going, or in dancing, which is done with great inequality and uncomeliness.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":13,"text":"So - No less incident are wise and pious speeches from a foolish and ungodly man.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":14,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":15,"text":"Bindeth - Whereby he hinders his own design of throwing the stone out of it.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":16,"text":"So - No less absurd is he that giveth to a fool that honour which he is not capable of using aright.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":17,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":18,"text":"A thorn - As a thorn is in a drunkard's hand, which he cannot manage cautiously, but employs to his own and others hurt.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":19,"text":"So - As unprofitable, and, by accident, hurtful to himself and others.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":20,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":21,"text":"Rewardeth - Will certainly give that recompence which is deserved by fools and transgressors, by such as sin either thro' ignorance, or wilfully.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":22,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":23,"text":"Turneth - Moving hither and thither upon it, but not removing from its place.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":24,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":25,"text":"A reason - A satisfactory reason of ail their actions.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":26,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":27,"text":"He - Who is going upon the way.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":28,"text":"With strife - In which he is not concerned, nor any way obliged to meddle.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":29,"text":"That taketh - Exposes himself to needless hazard.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":30,"text":"18.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":31,"text":"And death - Any instruments of death.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":32,"text":"23.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":33,"text":"Burning - With malice or hatred: A slanderous or evil tongue.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":34,"text":"Dross - Such a tongue and heart are of no real worth, although sometimes they make a shew of it, as dross does of silver.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":35,"text":"26.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":36,"text":"Deceit - With false professions of love.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":37,"text":"27.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":27,"scriptureVerseEnd":27},{"verse":38,"text":"Rolleth - Up the hill with design to do mischief to some person.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":27,"scriptureVerseEnd":27}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":26}}